  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Recall the formula&nbsp;of induced E.M.F. in terms of the length of the rod, and uniform magnetic field,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>B</mi><mi>v</mi><mi>l</mi></math>, here in the case of the ring,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi></math>,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>B</mi><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi></math>, when half ring enters,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>.</p>",
